t as the authority for my game design.\n\n3. FIX THE REAL PROBLEM: VISUALS BREAKING DURING MOVEMENT\n\nThe approved camera views are improving, but the scenery looks significantly worse when Benny swims forward or turns.\n\nPlease fix:\n\n- Stretched and smeared water textures.\n- Repeated or mirrored scenery.\n- Jagged seams and duplicated river surfaces.\n- Flat-looking water.\n- Gold rings or washer walls blocking the camera.\n- Incorrect tunnel curvature.\n- Missing scenery when the camera moves.\n- Floating or overlapping geometry.\n- Camera clipping.\n- Inconsistent lighting and reflections.\n- Incorrect foam and bubble placement.\n\nDo not solve these problems by simply placing a flat picture in front of the camera.\n\nUse properly fitted real 3D geometry, UV-mapped textures, depth-aware materials, and camera-consistent artwork projection.\n\nBuild matching textures for surfaces that become visible as Benny moves.\n\n4. RECREATE THE APPROVED VISUAL DETAILS\n\nFor every screen, compare the actual game to my approved reference.\n\nMatch:\n\n- Exact scenery composition and proportions.\n- Washer tunnel architecture.\n- Purple and gold metallic materials.\n- Bright cyan-and-magenta flowing water.\n- Glossy highlights and reflections.\n- Lighting and depth.\n- Foam, bubbles, and splashes.\n- Gold rings and mechanical fixtures.\n- Collectible coin placement.\n- Benny's original pink fur, round body, knitted hat, pom-pom, star, and splash.\n- Camera position and perspective.\n\nDo not add unnecessary decorations or invent new scenery.\n\n5. FIX EACH PLAYABLE SCREEN\n\nSCREEN 04: Correct the gold tunnel, glowing blue arrows, water thickness, foam, and moving-camera textures.\n\nSCREEN 05: Maintain the approved S-shaped river, purple washer walls, gold rings, lighting, and water effects while Benny moves.\n\nSCREEN 06 — MAJOR PRIORITY: Fix the oversized flat-looking blue water, repeated streaks, missing tunnel architecture, and camera movement. The entire environment should retain the beautiful curved 3D appearance of my approved image.\n\nSCREEN 07: Fix close-up walls, distorted gold rings, mirrored water, foam, and the transition into Screen 08.\n\nSCREEN 08: Preserve the successful scenery reconstruction while correcting moving-camera seams, duplicated river surfaces, gold-band clipping, coin spacing, and Benny's appearance.\n\n6. USE MY EXISTING SPECIALIST AGENTS\n\nI already have specialist agents working on my approved screens.\n\nContinue their existing work using their newest saved GitHub branches.\n\nMy current lead branch is:\n\n\"ccr-067047f0-up5d1m\"\n\nRepository:\n\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nUse separate specialist workstreams where my Claude usage allows.\n\nDo not restart successful reconstructions, overwrite existing work, or merge unfinished branches.\n\nPrioritize Screen 06's moving scenery and Screen 08's remaining issues, while ensuring Screens 04, 05, and 07 are also completed.\n\n7. MEASURE ACTUAL MOVING-GAMEPLAY QUALITY\n\nFor each screen, capture and compare:\n\n1. My original approved image.\n2. The current game at the matching camera position.\n3. Benny moving forward.\n4. Benny steering left.\n5. Benny steering right.\n6. Benny traveling through the entire screen.\n\nCheck visual accuracy at multiple positions along the actual path.\n\nA 98% fixed-camera color match does not mean the whole playable screen is 98% visually accurate.\n\nI WANT AT LEAST 8.5/10 VISUAL QUALITY THROUGHOUT GAMEPLAY, NOT JUST IN A STILL SCREENSHOT.\n\nUse consistent visual QA criteria. Report shortcomings honestly and distinguish subjective ratings from measured pixel similarity.\n\n8. USE THE BEST AVAILABLE TOOLS\n\nContinue using:\n\n- Blender for real 3D geometry and UV mapping.\n- Three.js/WebGL for the actual game.\n- Original approved artwork for texture matching.\n- Image-Blaster and fal.ai for controlled image cleanup when needed.\n- World Labs Marble for useful existing assets and materials.\n- Camera-fitting and visual-comparison scripts.\n- Playwright and Android testing tools.\n\nIf the current projection method cannot solve a particular moving-camera problem, investigate better geometry, UV mapping, depth-aware texture projection, and additional approved-style texture views before recommending further paid generations.\n\nDo not purchase additional credits or run new paid World Labs Marble or fal.ai jobs without my approval.\n\n9. PRESERVE ALL MY WORK\n\nKeep my original approved images unchanged.\n\nSave all successful improvements, scripts, assets, textures, camera settings, tests, and APK builds to GitHub.\n\nMaintain separate branches and frequent verified backups.\n\nDo not mark any screen approved until I personally approve it.\n\n10. WHAT I WANT YOU TO DO NOW\n\nSTART WITH A VISUAL-ACCURACY AUDIT OF SCREENS 04–08.\n\nIdentify the biggest moving-camera visual problem on each screen and the exact technical cause.\n\nThen fix the highest-impact problems using the existing 3D reconstruction, without rebuilding the project.\n\nShow me each improved screen separately at full portrait size, with approved-versus-new comparisons and moving-gameplay views.\n\nGive me a realistic visual rating for each screen and continue improving the visuals toward at least 8.5/10, preferably 9/10 or better.\n\nDO NOT WORK ON MY GOOGLE FLOW OPENING OR ENDING VIDEOS.\n\nDO NOT REDESIGN MY APPROVED SCREENS.\n\nDO NOT SPEND MARBLE OR FAL.AI CREDITS WITHOUT MY APPROVAL.\n\nMY NUMBER-ONE PRIORITY IS MAKING ALL FIVE REAL PLAYABLE 3D SCREENS LOOK AS CLOSE AS POSSIBLE TO MY ORIGINAL APPROVED ARTWORK, EVEN WHILE BENNY IS SWIMMING THROUGH THEM.\n\nPlease begin using my existing project and specialist work immediately.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T21:49:30.235Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
