{"clientPlatform": "android", "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-4bd35b15-7z45t0", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": "@\"/root/.claude/uploads/cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a/49cef2b8-Rainbow_Restore_Next_Claude_Complete.txt\" @\"/root/.claude/uploads/cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a/b4a13988-Rainbow_Restore_Next_Claude_Complete.md\"  CLAUDIA — URGENT: GET ALL FIVE RAINBOW GAME SCREENS TO AT LEAST 8.5/10 VISUAL QUALITY\n\nI want you to focus on the VISUAL ACCURACY of my original approved Rainbow game screens.\n\nMY MINIMUM TARGET IS 8.5/10 VISUAL QUALITY, IDEALLY 9–9.5/10.\n\nI do not want you to redesign my game or create different scenery. I want the actual playable 3D game to look as close as technically possible to my ORIGINAL APPROVED IMAGES.\n\n1. DO NOT WORK ON MY GOOGLE FLOW VIDEO SCENES\n\nScreens 01–03 are Google Flow opening videos, including the cartoon girl and the pink character with the crazy eyes.\n\nScreens 09–11 are Google Flow ending videos involving the girl and Benny returning to the towel.\n\nDO NOT SPEND DEVELOPMENT TIME OR MARBLE CREDITS RECONSTRUCTING THOSE VIDEO SCENES.\n\nOnly focus on these five playable 3D Android screens:\n\n- Screen 04 — Through the Five Arrows\n- Screen 05 — Flow Into the Current\n- Screen 06 — Crest the Rinse Arch\n- Screen 07 — Dive the Washer Tube\n- Screen 08 — Final Spin Chamber\n\n2. WORLD LABS MARBLE — CHECK WHAT IT CAN ACTUALLY DO\n\nI need you to determine whether World Labs Marble can genuinely help us achieve my approved visual quality.\n\nPrevious Marble tests recreated the general colors and materials but changed the depth, architecture, and layout of my approved scenery.\n\nPlease verify the existing World Labs connection using free checks only.\n\nDO NOT GENERATE NEW MARBLE WORLDS OR SPEND CREDITS YET.\n\nEvaluate whether existing Marble splats, meshes, panoramas, and materials can improve our current 3D environments.\n\nIf Marble cannot accurately reproduce my approved screen layouts, do not keep spending credits trying the same method.\n\nUse Marble as a supporting asset resource where useful—not as the authority for my game design.\n\n3. FIX THE REAL PROBLEM: VISUALS BREAKING DURING MOVEMENT\n\nThe approved camera views are improving, but the scenery looks significantly worse when Benny swims forward or turns.\n\nPlease fix:\n\n- Stretched and smeared water textures.\n- Repeated or mirrored scenery.\n- Jagged seams and duplicated river surfaces.\n- Flat-looking water.\n- Gold rings or washer walls blocking the camera.\n- Incorrect tunnel curvature.\n- Missing scenery when the camera moves.\n- Floating or overlapping geometry.\n- Camera clipping.\n- Inconsistent lighting and reflections.\n- Incorrect foam and bubble placement.\n\nDo not solve these problems by simply placing a flat picture in front of the camera.\n\nUse properly fitted real 3D geometry, UV-mapped textures, depth-aware materials, and camera-consistent artwork projection.\n\nBuild matching textures for surfaces that become visible as Benny moves.\n\n4. RECREATE THE APPROVED VISUAL DETAILS\n\nFor every screen, compare the actual game to my approved reference.\n\nMatch:\n\n- Exact scenery composition and proportions.\n- Washer tunnel architecture.\n- Purple and gold metallic materials.\n- Bright cyan-and-magenta flowing water.\n- Glossy highlights and reflections.\n- Lighting and depth.\n- Foam, bubbles, and splashes.\n- Gold rings and mechanical fixtures.\n- Collectible coin placement.\n- Benny's original pink fur, round body, knitted hat, pom-pom, star, and splash.\n- Camera position and perspective.\n\nDo not add unnecessary decorations or invent new scenery.\n\n5. FIX EACH PLAYABLE SCREEN\n\nSCREEN 04: Correct the gold tunnel, glowing blue arrows, water thickness, foam, and moving-camera textures.\n\nSCREEN 05: Maintain the approved S-shaped river, purple washer walls, gold rings, lighting, and water effects while Benny moves.\n\nSCREEN 06 — MAJOR PRIORITY: Fix the oversized flat-looking blue water, repeated streaks, missing tunnel architecture, and camera movement. The entire environment should retain the beautiful curved 3D appearance of my approved image.\n\nSCREEN 07: Fix close-up walls, distorted gold rings, mirrored water, foam, and the transition into Screen 08.\n\nSCREEN 08: Preserve the successful scenery reconstruction while correcting moving-camera seams, duplicated river surfaces, gold-band clipping, coin spacing, and Benny's appearance.\n\n6. USE MY EXISTING SPECIALIST AGENTS\n\nI already have specialist agents working on my approved screens.\n\nContinue their existing work using their newest saved GitHub branches.\n\nMy current lead branch is:\n\n\"ccr-067047f0-up5d1m\"\n\nRepository:\n\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nUse separate specialist workstreams where my Claude usage allows.\n\nDo not restart successful reconstructions, overwrite existing work, or merge unfinished branches.\n\nPrioritize Screen 06's moving scenery and Screen 08's remaining issues, while ensuring Screens 04, 05, and 07 are also completed.\n\n7. MEASURE ACTUAL MOVING-GAMEPLAY QUALITY\n\nFor each screen, capture and compare:\n\n1. My original approved image.\n2. The current game at the matching camera position.\n3. Benny moving forward.\n4. Benny steering left.\n5. Benny steering right.\n6. Benny traveling through the entire screen.\n\nCheck visual accuracy at multiple positions along the actual path.\n\nA 98% fixed-camera color match does not mean the whole playable screen is 98% visually accurate.\n\nI WANT AT LEAST 8.5/10 VISUAL QUALITY THROUGHOUT GAMEPLAY, NOT JUST IN A STILL SCREENSHOT.\n\nUse consistent visual QA criteria. Report shortcomings honestly and distinguish subjective ratings from measured pixel similarity.\n\n8. USE THE BEST AVAILABLE TOOLS\n\nContinue using:\n\n- Blender for real 3D geometry and UV mapping.\n- Three.js/WebGL for the actual game.\n- Original approved artwork for texture matching.\n- Image-Blaster and fal.ai for controlled image cleanup when needed.\n- World Labs Marble for useful existing assets and materials.\n- Camera-fitting and visual-comparison scripts.\n- Playwright and Android testing tools.\n\nIf the current projection method cannot solve a particular moving-camera problem, investigate better geometry, UV mapping, depth-aware texture projection, and additional approved-style texture views before recommending further paid generations.\n\nDo not purchase additional credits or run new paid World Labs Marble or fal.ai jobs without my approval.\n\n9. PRESERVE ALL MY WORK\n\nKeep my original approved images unchanged.\n\nSave all successful improvements, scripts, assets, textures, camera settings, tests, and APK builds to GitHub.\n\nMaintain separate branches and frequent verified backups.\n\nDo not mark any screen approved until I personally approve it.\n\n10. WHAT I WANT YOU TO DO NOW\n\nSTART WITH A VISUAL-ACCURACY AUDIT OF SCREENS 04–08.\n\nIdentify the biggest moving-camera visual problem on each screen and the exact technical cause.\n\nThen fix the highest-impact problems using the existing 3D reconstruction, without rebuilding the project.\n\nShow me each improved screen separately at full portrait size, with approved-versus-new comparisons and moving-gameplay views.\n\nGive me a realistic visual rating for each screen and continue improving the visuals toward at least 8.5/10, preferably 9/10 or better.\n\nDO NOT WORK ON MY GOOGLE FLOW OPENING OR ENDING VIDEOS.\n\nDO NOT REDESIGN MY APPROVED SCREENS.\n\nDO NOT SPEND MARBLE OR FAL.AI CREDITS WITHOUT MY APPROVAL.\n\nMY NUMBER-ONE PRIORITY IS MAKING ALL FIVE REAL PLAYABLE 3D SCREENS LOOK AS CLOSE AS POSSIBLE TO MY ORIGINAL APPROVED ARTWORK, EVEN WHILE BENNY IS SWIMMING THROUGH THEM.\n\nPlease begin using my existing project and specialist work immediately.", "role": "user"}, "origin": {"kind": "human"}, "parentUuid": "b7d29430-2e88-44cc-9376-25aecfcfd074", "permissionMode": "default", "promptId": "c2bd140e-9d37-46ab-a98e-067e9dd2e702", "promptSource": "sdk", "savedFiles": [{"file_uuid": "49cef2b8-43b7-46dd-9dd9-bd25b22045d2", "inlined": false, "path": "/root/.claude/uploads/cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a/49cef2b8-Rainbow_Restore_Next_Claude_Complete.txt"}, {"file_uuid": "b4a13988-0c35-4b18-b46f-088af4a5a2fc", "inlined": false, "path": "/root/.claude/uploads/cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a/b4a13988-Rainbow_Restore_Next_Claude_Complete.md"}], "sessionId": "cd1e5cfb-443e-5b5a-b9b8-262d44ab3b8a", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T21:49:30.921Z", "turnAttributionKey": "dddce5fc-57b5-4417-ab88-0f13b7b80f61", "turnOrigin": "human", "turnPosition": {"promptIndex": 1, "turnIndex": 1}, "type": "user", "userType": "external", "uuid": "dddce5fc-57b5-4417-ab88-0f13b7b80f61", "version": "2.1.326"}
{"attachment": {"content": {"file": {"content": "CLAUDIA — COMPLETE RAINBOW ANDROID GAME ACCOUNT TRANSFER, RECOVERY, SEVEN SPECIALIST WORKSTREAMS, TEN DESIGN/TECHNICAL AGENTS, WORLD LABS MARBLE, FAL.AI, GOOGLE FLOW AND CONTINUATION\n\nTHIS IS THE COMPLETE INSTRUCTION FILE. READ IT FROM START TO FINISH BEFORE WORKING.\n\nI have moved to this Claude account because my previous Claude account ran out of available usage credits. I already have an EXISTING Rainbow game. I am not authorizing a new game, a redesign, or a restart. Recover the newest actually saved work from GitHub, establish a safe new lead and specialist workspace, verify the tools and accounts, and continue from the exact saved checkpoint.\n\nMY TOP PRIORITY: make the VISUALS of my ORIGINAL APPROVED PLAYABLE SCREENS 04, 05, 06, 07 AND 08 look as close as technically possible to those original images. Target at least 8.5/10 when judged on real gameplay, ideally 9/10 or better, with ambitious near-95% fixed-camera fidelity where attainable. Do not represent a pixel-color-tolerance score as proof that the whole moving 3D level meets that standard. No creative redesign.\n\nIMPORTANT VIDEO EXCEPTION: Screens 01–03 (opening, including the girl and unusual-eyed pink character) and Screens 09–11 (ending with the girl and towel) will be GOOGLE FLOW VIDEOS supplied by me. Do NOT spend time generating them as playable 3D or spend video credits. Only Screens 04–08 are the real playable 3D Android gameplay I want reconstructed. Preserve existing fallback code and the flowplan hand-off, but do not make or purchase the Flow videos.\n\nREPOSITORY: https://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\nOWNER / REPO: josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\nPREVIOUS ACCOUNT'S LEAD BRANCH: ccr-f983b317-2vt0zh\nLAST INDEPENDENTLY CHECKED LEAD SHA (CHECKPOINT, NOT NECESSARILY LATEST): bba7034a404e7c739832fe0f9e313896c88df3e0\nCheck GitHub's LIVE remote branch tip at restoration time. It may have advanced by autosave.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. SAVE-FIRST RULE — DON'T DAMAGE WHAT EXISTS\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Connect this Claude account to the EXISTING private GitHub repository. GitHub connection and app permissions require my explicit action if they are not already configured. There is only ONE repository; branches are NOT separate repositories.\n2. Before any code changes, fetch all branches and inspect the latest remote SHA for the lead, preview, and all seven specialist branches. Record commit SHA, author date, and the last real code/milestone commit separately from transcript-only autosaves.\n3. Check if old-account sessions could still be running or waking on reset; do NOT let two sessions write to the same branch. Never change or force-push an older branch.\n4. Reconstruct the current state from remote files, approved references, LFS assets, QA notes, status files and saved transcripts. Do not assume that unseen/uncommitted work from closed containers is recoverable.\n5. Create a NEW isolated lead branch for this account (a fresh ccr-* or equivalent), from the newest VERIFIED lead tip; record its parent SHA. Preserve ccr-f983b317-2vt0zh unchanged. NEVER start from the stale GitHub default branch.\n6. Do not reset, rebase, squash, cherry-pick, merge, close PRs, or overwrite successful work without my express approval. The one old approved combination was on a protected TEST PREVIEW BRANCH ONLY, not a blanket authorization to merge source branches.\n7. Before anything expensive, restore and verify the 5-minute autosave for every ACTIVE session, including manual save before stopping, remote-vs-local SHA comparison, and recovery notes. Autosave only works while the cloud environment/session is active; do not claim it runs when stopped.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. ALL EIGHT DEVELOPMENT BRANCHES — ONE LEAD + SEVEN WORKSTREAMS\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\nThese are the latest known ACCOUNT 5 / ROUND 5 branches. Fetch the NEWEST live remote tips, not just the SHA values below.\n\nROLE                         EXISTING BRANCH                                LAST OBSERVED SHA (NOT FINAL)\nLead Claudia                 ccr-f983b317-2vt0zh                            bba7034a404e7c739832fe0f9e313896c88df3e0\n08 scenery while swimming     claude/rainbow-s08-scenery-c5                    700f09e16ca0e44394a9926cd6a261541a645cad\n08 Benny appearance           claude/rainbow-s08-benny08-bake-c5               ae7abe5bc4d34193d28a1f55c498e87573699a40\n08 camera/obstructions        claude/rainbow-s08-camclear-c5                   18687513e3a35e553472a05ae7fb626c2f8108ce\n07 Washer Tube               claude/rainbow-s07-match-c5                     835a72dbb5abad1067b538c79b1f759b06e2cbeb\n06 Rinse Arch                claude/rainbow-s06-match-c5                     c088718bb9e3374583238f4ee93f25bdee600065\n05 Flow Into the Current     claude/rainbow-s05-match-c5                     ebaf6cac71812ad5c00a9088ba48b6febdb42b2b\n04 Through the Five Arrows   claude/rainbow-s04-match-c5                     d1e422faff67a37f837566301fb8abff0bac98db\n\nONE MORE VALUABLE BRANCH:\nCombined read-only/review preview: claude/rainbow-preview-all-c5\nLast observed SHA: 965e4ef903e4905db48bb52f064d11b23916d938\nThis preview branch is NOT yet approved for production; it contains cross-screen switch conflicts. Preserve it as a diagnostic and recovery point.\n\nOn this NEW account, after reading the handoff, create separate -c6 continuation branches ONLY where an agent will actually resume work, from the newest -c5 tip for each role. These new branches must be separate isolated cloud sessions/worktrees. Do not push to -c5 or older protected branches. A paused agent's -c6 branch may be prepared without starting a new expensive session. Verify no duplicate live writers, including prior-account sessions.\n\nOLD HISTORIC BRANCHES MUST REMAIN ACCESSIBLE AND UNMODIFIED, including -c4/-c3/-c2 workstreams, ccr-067047f0-up5d1m, ccr-c0235034-ks6sx3, ccr-d4240b15-rl1i72, ccr-9c4a8ad6-xovgsx, ccr-b0757dec-dj6l1o (older Screen 05 line B), and codex/* experiments. They can hold irreplaceable prior images, textures, code, comparisons, and backups. NO automatic merges.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. START BY READING THESE SAVED PROJECT INSTRUCTIONS\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\nRead these files from the NEWEST lead branch in this order (newer decisions override stale older notes):\n1. CLAUDE.md\n2. TOP of docs/NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_HANDOFF.md — section titled ACCOUNT 5 (round 5) STATE + \"STATE AT THE USER'S SAVE EVERYTHING ORDER\"\n3. docs/PARALLEL_PROGRESS.md — ROUND 5 first; older rounds as supporting history\n4. docs/briefs/2026-11-17-r5/COMMON_RULES.md and docs/briefs/2026-11-17-r5/USER_DECISIONS.md\n5. docs/briefs/2026-11-17-r5/S08_SCENERY.md and S08_BENNY.md\n6. docs/briefs/2026-11-17-r5/REPORTS_ROUND5.md\n7. docs/briefs/2026-11-17-r4/USER_DECISIONS.md and all relevant r4 S*.md briefs\n8. docs/FLOW_VIDEO.md\n9. qa/lead_r5/2026-11-17/README.md\n10. qa/screen_videos/2026-11-17/COMPARISON.md and rainbow_all_screens_APPROVED_vs_NOW.mp4\n11. backups/AGENTS_STATUS.json, backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json, backups/BOOTSTRAP_REPORT.md, backups/BACKUP_LOG.md\n12. qa/match/<screen>/NOTES.md and each specialist's newest STATUS.md, SHARED_CHANGES.md, measurements, comparison pictures, and preview test switches.\n\nImportant: an earlier backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md describes old branches and is HISTORICAL, not the current starting point. Existing session IDs in saved briefs refer to OLD accounts; never send messages to them expecting to manage a new account. On your new sessions use their NEW IDs and update coordination documents accordingly.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n4. THE TEN EXIST