even of the nine visually painted 08 coins; those seven are auto-credited. DO NOT silently change the cinematic handoff or coins; flag this for my approval. Don't count a `goto('08')` QA jump as proof of a full game run. The saved A–E flowplan tests had an end-to-end 91/2,240 pass after correcting test-harness timing; rerun on newest code.\n119\t\n120\t-------------------------------------------------------------------\n121\t7. VISUAL QUALITY TARGET AND HOW TO JUDGE IT\n122\t-------------------------------------------------------------------\n123\tI care MOST about appearance, not making new mechanics. Every playable screen must match its OWN original approved image as closely as technically possible: composition, geometry, perspective, glossy pink/cyan water, purple/gold walls and rings, foam, bubbles, lighting, reflections, depth, Benny, HUD and coins.\n124\t\n125\tMy minimum desired visual quality is 8.5/10 throughout gameplay, ideally 9/10 or more. Work toward near-95% reference matching at the approved locked camera where technically achievable, but recognize the user-visible whole-frame scores may be lower. Do not promise perfect 100% 3D identity or claim high scores just because one fixed-camera color tolerance is high.\n126\t\n127\tFor EVERY important screen change show 1 APPROVED ORIGINAL, 2 BEFORE, 3 NEW as THREE SEPARATE LARGE FULL-SIZE PORTRAIT IMAGES, not a collage, plus separately presented forward and left/right steering views. Match resolution and framing; report scenery-only, Benny+effects and whole-frame metrics; call out differences honestly. Motion must preserve material continuity: no mirrored tiles, flat-looking blue planes, jagged seams, repeated river, clipping gold arcs, disappearing tunnel, giant occluding walls, or wrong water form.\n128\t\n129\tUse original approved pixels on correct fitted geometry and proper UV/depth-aware world-anchored materials. When new surfaces become visible while the camera moves, make convincing matching texture