-----------------------------------\n224\t16. GAMEPLAY AND FLOWPLAN REGRESSION CHECKS — PROTECT THE VISUAL WORK\n225\t-------------------------------------------------------------------\n226\tRun typecheck, continuity, gameplay and Flow video-handoff regression checks on the recovered lead without turning unfinished test switches into production defaults.\n227\t* Gameplay baseline: 8/8, 91 coins, total 2,240, 07→08 drop roughly 61.4 units. Keep pickups, steering, collisions, hearts and HUD working.\n228\t* Google Flow: `node scripts/flowplan-test.mjs` checks A–E, including a TRUE full ride to exact 91/2,240 with approved 01–03 / 04–08 / 09–11 split. Do not treat a QA `goto` jump with 2,230 as an actual game coin total.\n229\t* Use deterministic capture methods and compare unchanged build twice to distinguish animation noise from real code differences. Preserve source URL switches and hidden variants.\n230\t* Never claim real-phone performance or visual success from headless Chromium alone.\n231\t\n232\t-------------------------------------------------------------------\n233\t17. PROJECT BACKUPS AND RECOVERY WHEN CREDITS RUN LOW\n234\t-------------------------------------------------------------------\n235\tActivate the repository's five-minute autosave only while the session is alive; verify status with `python3 -I scripts/autosave-status.py` and direct git remote SHAs. Use `scripts/rainbow-autosave.py --reason manual:end` at safe exit, confirm all intended files are pushed, and don't allow secrets in commits.\n236\t\n237\tAt EVERY milestone: update each agent's STATUS.md / NOTES.md / SHARED_CHANGES.md, exact next task, committed files, screenshot paths, APK paths, test results, and the full SHA of its own branch. Lead updates `docs/PARALLEL_PROGRESS.md`, `docs/NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_HANDOFF.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `backups/AGENTS_STATUS.json`, and an updated branch map so a future Claude account can restore the work again.\n238\t\n239\tIf account usage warns, prioritize back